A||N||3||DaveL||Battery Causes Haunted Car Syndrome||||12||
Z||000000||DaveL||09-21-2000||04:03 PM||||Well, I've been having a lot of different odd things happening electrically with my 87 SE 2.5 DIS. I kept getting odd codes occasionally with no apparent ill effects to the car, including the code 24 (I think) having been set while not moving. The CES light always went off after a few seconds. Recently at night I began to notice that my instrument lights would sometimes get dimmer with any slowing in idle. Well, I got up yesterday and went out to start the kart and it almost turned over once before dying in a rash of clicks. Took the battery out and found a 6 year old Die Hard with a cracked case. It has been leaking acid all over the battery tray, and on some of the little connections at the wheel well area near the battery. There is a bad buildup of white crystalline looking stuff. I put in the new battery, and not only does it run different and start different, I haven't had any Check eng soon lights at all! Guess I'll have to take it back out this weekend and clean all that gunk out. Baking soda is the best thing to use right?||||reg||12
